    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Scherrer (1918) showed that tiny crystallites give broadened powder lines, with width \beta=K\lambda/(\tau\cos\theta) for crystallite size \tau. scherrer_crystallite_size inverts this: here, copper powder patterns are broadened for three crystallite sizes, and each size is recovered from the measured width of the (111) line.">

